        "content": "<p>I'm trying to use an expression of the form <code>change a with b</code> and got this error message:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">Tactic</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`Lean.Parser.Tactic.changeWith</span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">has</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">not</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">been</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">implemented</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>What does it mean?</p>",
        "id": 580794134,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Novak",
        "timestamp": 1774079219
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>O.k, turns out this feature just wasn't developed yet (but for some reason it's  mentioned in the documentation), there are alternatives mentioned in the answer here:<br>\n<a href=\"https://proofassistants.stackexchange.com/questions/4967/lean4-tactic-has-not-been-implemented\">https://proofassistants.stackexchange.com/questions/4967/lean4-tactic-has-not-been-implemented</a></p>",
        "id": 580794788,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Novak",
        "timestamp": 1774079895
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Where did you find it in the documentation? In the docstring itself? We should probably remove that. Cc <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"238446\">@Anne Baanen</span></p>",
